We need to allocate vehicle to SCB: allocate_vehicle_unit SCB VUG (requires candidate_prepared SCB, not vehicle_allocated SCB, vehicle_available VUG). VUG currently allocated to SCA; we need to make it available via dispatch of SCA (as discussed). So we need to dispatch SCA first (which will make vehicle_available VUG true, dispatched SCA true). Then allocate to SCB.

Now we also need to allocate dispatch slot to OA, DA, SCA. We'll need to allocate dispatch slot, then execute dispatch (which makes dispatched true, vehicle_available, dispatch_slot_available). We'll need to do this for each candidate in some order.

Goal also wants dispatch_ready for each candidate (OA, DA, SCA). dispatch_ready is set by actions: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready (for origin availability), mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready (for destination), and also dispatch_ready is set automatically for SCA? Actually init has dispatch_ready SCA true. For OA and DA we need to make them dispatch_ready via those mark actions. Precondition: origin_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. So we need transport leg assembled and loading authorized before we can mark dispatch ready for OA and DA.

Thus we need to assemble transport leg, load origin payload (makes origin leg loaded), authorize transport leg loading (action authorize_transport_leg_loading). After that we can mark origin availability dispatch ready and destination availability dispatch ready.

But note: mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed (we will have after locking). Also requires transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized. Similarly for destination.

Thus we need to have transport leg assembled and loading authorized before we can mark OA and DA dispatch ready.

Now we also need to load container beta onto transport leg (loading_container_leg_linked LCB TLA and loading_container_loaded LCB). This requires loading_container_loaded LCB (we need to load container onto leg via load_container_onto_leg). Precondition: candidate_prepared ?candidate (schedule_candidate), candidate_transport_leg_linked ?candidate ?transport_leg, candidate_loading_container_linked ?candidate ?loading_container, loading_container_available ?loading_container, transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg, not loading_container_loaded ?loading_container. Effect: loading_container_loaded ?loading_container, loading_container_leg_linked ?loading_container ?transport_leg, not loading_container_available ?loading_container.

Thus we need a schedule_candidate (presumably SCB) that has loading_container_linked (we have SCB linked to LCB), candidate_prepared SCB, candidate_transport_leg_linked SCB TLA (true), loading_container_available LCB (init true), transport_leg_assembled TLA (we need to assemble), transport_leg_loading_authorized TLA (need to authorize), not loading_container_loaded LCB (init false). So after we assemble leg and authorize loading, we can load container onto leg via SCB.

Thus we need to have SCB prepared, with loading container linked, etc., before we can load container onto leg.

Now we also need to have origin leg loaded (origin_leg_loaded TLA true) for confirm_equipment_assignment (for SCB). We can achieve origin leg loaded via assemble_origin_loaded_leg (which requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_node_occupied, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available). Wait let's check assemble_origin_loaded_leg precondition:

(:action assemble_origin_loaded_leg
    :parameters (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?destination_node - destination_node ?transport_leg - transport_leg)
    :precondition
      (and
        (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability)
        (destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability)
        (origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node)
        (destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node)
        (origin_node_occupied ?origin_node)
        (destination_node_ready ?destination_node)
        (not
          (origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability))
        (destination_availability_confirmed ?destination_availability)
        (transport_leg_available ?transport_leg)
      )
    :effect
      (and
        (transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg)
        (transport_leg_origin_linked ?transport_leg ?origin_node)
        (transport_leg_destination_linked ?transport_leg ?destination_node)
        (origin_leg_loaded ?transport_leg)
        (not
          (transport_leg_available ?transport_leg)
        )
      )
)

Thus to assemble origin loaded leg we need origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_node_occupied, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed false, destination_availability_confirmed true, transport_leg_available.

Similarly assemble_destination_loaded_leg requires origin_node_ready, destination_node_occupied, origin_availability_confirmed true, destination_availability_confirmed false.

Assemble_fully_loaded_leg requires both origin_node_occupied and destination_node_occupied, both availabilities not confirmed.

Thus we have multiple ways to get transport leg assembled and origin leg loaded.

Given we need origin leg loaded and destination leg not loaded (for confirm_equipment_assignment). So we can use assemble_origin_loaded_leg (which sets origin_leg_loaded true, destination leg not loaded). That requires origin_node_occupied, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed false, destination_availability_confirmed true.

Thus we need to have:
- origin_availability_locked OA true
- origin_availability_confirmed OA false (temporarily)
- destination_availability_locked DA true
- destination_availability_confirmed DA true
- origin_node_occupied ONA true
- destination_node_ready DNA true
- transport_leg_available TLA true

After assembling origin loaded leg, we get transport_leg_assembled true, origin_leg_loaded true, transport_leg_origin_linked, transport_leg_destination_linked, and transport_leg_available becomes false.

Then we need to authorize transport leg loading (action authorize_transport_leg_loading) which requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we need origin_availability_locked OA true (still true), candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTPA true (we will have after attaching). So we can authorize.

After authorization, we have transport_leg_loading_authorized true.

Now we can load container onto leg via SCB (load_container_onto_leg). This requires candidate_prepared SCB, candidate_transport_leg_linked SCB TLA, candidate_loading_container_linked SCB LCB, loading_container_available LCB (still true before loading), transport_leg_assembled TLA (true after assemble), transport_leg_loading_authorized TLA (true after authorize), not loading_container_loaded LCB (true before loading). After loading, we get loading_container_loaded LCB true, loading_container_leg_linked LCB TLA true, loading_container_available LCB false.

Now we need to confirm equipment assignment for SCB (confirm_equipment_assignment). Precondition includes:
- candidate_prepared SCB
- candidate_loading_container_linked SCB LCB
- loading_container_loaded LCB
- loading_container_leg_linked LCB TLA
- candidate_task_profile_linked SCB RTPA
- origin_leg_loaded TLA (true after assemble_origin_loaded_leg)
- equipment_reserved SCB
- candidate_equipment_linked SCB ?equipment_resource
- not candidate_staged_for_loading SCB

Thus we need to reserve equipment resource for SCB and link it. There's action reserve_equipment_resource (parameters ?candidate - schedule_candidate ?equipment_resource - equipment_resource). Precondition: candidate_prepared ?candidate, equipment_available ?equipment_resource, not equipment_reserved ?candidate. Effect: equipment_reserved ?candidate, candidate_equipment_linked ?candidate ?equipment_resource, not equipment_available ?equipment_resource.

Thus we need to reserve an equipment resource (either ERA or ERB) for SCB before confirm_equipment_assignment. After reserving, we have candidate_equipment_linked SCB to that resource.

Then confirm_equipment_assignment will set candidate_staged_for_loading SCB true and equipment_confirmed SCB true.

Thus after confirm_equipment_assignment we have candidate_staged_for_loading SCB true (goal), equipment_confirmed SCB true (not required but okay).

Now we also need candidate_operator_linked SCB OP and candidate_skill_certificate_linked SCB SCA_CERT. We'll need to assign operator and skill certificate to SCB (after we have candidate_prepared SCB). Assign operator requires candidate_prepared SCB and operator_available. Assign skill certificate requires candidate_prepared SCB and skill_certificate_available.

Thus we need to prepare SCB (candidate_prepared SCB). To prepare SCB we need candidate_created SCB (true), vehicle_allocated SCB? Actually prepare requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated? Wait confirm_candidate_preparedness precondition: candidate_created ?candidate, vehicle_allocated ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not candidate_prepared ?candidate. So we need vehicle_allocated SCB (we will allocate after we free VUG), candidate_task_profile_linked SCB RTPA (we need to attach task profile to SCB), and not candidate_prepared SCB (init false). So we need to allocate vehicle to SCB, attach task profile, then confirm preparedness.

Thus order for SCB:
- Ensure vehicle_available VUG (we will get after dispatching SCA)
- allocate_vehicle_unit SCB VUG
- attach_task_profile SCB RTPA (requires candidate_prepared? Actually attach_task_profile requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, route_task_profile_available. So we need vehicle_allocated first, then attach task profile.)
- confirm_candidate_preparedness SCB RTPA (makes candidate_prepared true)
- assign_operator_resource SCB OP (requires candidate_prepared SCB, operator_available)
- assign_skill_certificate SCB SCA_CERT (requires candidate_prepared SCB, skill_certificate_available)
- (maybe also need to reserve equipment and confirm equipment assignment later)
- Also need to ensure candidate_loading_container_linked SCB LCB (already true)
- Need to load container onto leg (requires SCB prepared etc)
- Need to reserve equipment resource (ERA or ERB) for SCB
- Need to confirm equipment assignment (which will set candidate_staged_for_loading true)
- Also need to have transport leg assembled and loading authorized before loading container onto leg (as earlier)
- Also need to have origin leg loaded (via assemble_origin_loaded_leg) before loading container onto leg? Actually load_container_onto_leg does not require origin leg loaded; only requires transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we can load container after we have assembled leg and authorized loading, regardless of origin leg loaded. However confirm_equipment_assignment requires origin_leg_loaded true. So we need origin leg loaded before confirm_equipment_assignment. So we need to assemble origin loaded leg (which sets origin_leg_loaded true) before confirm_equipment_assignment. The load_container_onto_leg can happen before or after origin leg loaded? It requires transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized (both true after assemble origin loaded leg and authorize). So we can do: assemble origin loaded leg, authorize loading, load container onto leg, then confirm equipment assignment (which requires origin_leg_loaded true, loading_container_loaded, etc). That works.

Now we also need to achieve destination availability locked/confirmed, destination node occupied/ready, dispatch allocated/ready/dispatched for DA.

We also need to achieve origin availability locked/confirmed, origin node occupied/ready, dispatch allocated/ready/dispatched for OA.

We also need to achieve dispatch allocated/ready/dispatched for SCA